The synonym "corpus gastricum (ventriculare)" is a Latin term for the body of the stomach. While it refers to the same anatomical structure, it is not used interchangeably with "body of stomach" in everyday biomedical language, which typically uses English terms. The use of Latin terms can introduce ambiguity and is not a common linguistic variant in biomedical text. Therefore, the relationship is "related".
